            <div xml:id="d929">

                <pb facs="0866" n="762" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg762"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6606.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Ciudad
                            Porfirio Díaz to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Ciudad Porfirio Díaz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 10, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Governor of Coahuila, at Monclova, and Colonel Carranza, here, have just
                    seized the rolling stock shops and their equipment and other property of the
                    Mexican National Railway lines here. Evidently they intend to attempt to operate
                    all the railroad and shops for the benefit of the State cause.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Luther T. Ellsworth</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
